The Amidah blessing for prosperity is called Barech Aleinu (“Bless for us”). It focuses on sustenance, livelihood, and material blessing. Here is a clear English version:

Amidah – Prayer for Prosperity (Barech Aleinu)

Bless for us, Lord our God, this year and all its kinds of produce for good.

Grant blessing upon the face of the earth,
and satisfy us from Your goodness.

Bless our year like the good years.
Blessed are You, Lord,
who blesses the years.
========================================================================
Slightly expanded traditional-style translation:

Bless for us, O Lord our God, this year and all its produce for good;
grant blessing upon the face of the earth;
satisfy us with Your goodness;
and bless our year like the best of years.

Blessed are You, Lord,
who blesses the years.

This blessing reflects both physical sustenance (food, livelihood) and overall well-being.

If you want, I can continue with the next blessings (like ingathering of exiles, justice, or peace) or give you the full Amidah in order.
